 **Algorithm Steps:**
-1. **Evaluate Base Turbulence**: Calculate the turbulence value at the texture point: $\text{turb} = \text{fast\_turbulence}(\text{pnt})$. Map this to a base density using the power table. The index is calculated as: $\text{idx} = \lfloor \text{turb} \times 0.5 \times (\text{POW\_TABLE\_SIZE} - 1) \rfloor$. The density is set to $\text{pow\_table}[\text{idx}]$ [S1, unofficial].
-2. **Calculate Spherical Distance Factor**: Compute the vector from the volume center to the world point: $\text{diff} = \text{pnt\_world} - \text{vol.shape.center}$. Compute the squared distance: $\text{dist\_sq} = \text{diff} \cdot \text{diff}$. Scale by the inverse squared radius to get a normalized distance factor: $\text{density\_max} = \text{dist\_sq} \times \text{vol.shape.inv\_rad\_sq.y}$ [S1, unofficial].
-3. **Add Spatial Noise Offset**: Calculate an index into the offset table based on the sum of the texture point coordinates: $\text{indx} = \lfloor (\text{pnt}.x + \text{pnt}.y + \text{pnt}.z) \times 100 \rfloor \ \& \ (\text{OFFSET\_SIZE} - 1)$. Add the noise offset scaled by `parms[3]`: $\text{density\_max} += \text{parms}[3] \times \text{offset}[\text{indx}]$ [S1, unofficial].
-4. **Apply Cosine Ramp Falloff**: If `density_max` exceeds the threshold $0.25$ (25% from center), compute the ramp index: $i = \lfloor (\text{density\_max} - 0.25) \times \frac{4}{3} \times \text{RAMP\_SIZE} \rfloor$. Clamp $i$ to the valid range: $i = \min(i, \text{RAMP\_SIZE} - 1)$. Retrieve the ramp value: $\text{ramp\_val} = \text{ramp}[i]$. Multiply the density by this factor: $\text{density} *= \text{ramp\_val}$ [S1, unofficial]. If `density_max` is less than $0.25$, the ramp is skipped and the base density remains unchanged [S1, unofficial].
